codex
I found a blocking operation left inside the PRC fix: every PRC call immediately executes `loss.detach().item()`, forcing a host/device synchronization. At proxy scale this happens hundreds of times (the prior smoke recorded 600 PRC calls), so the model forwards were batched but CUDA was still serialized into repeated futex waits. Reliability instrumentation has the same eager `.item()`/Python-bool pattern per class. I’m changing these counters to accumulate detached device scalars and synchronize only when a phase snapshot is emitted; training losses and gradients are untouched.
